// DataServiceClient is a client for the elephant.tables.v1.DataService service.
type DataServiceClient interface {
	// List reads a page of rows from a table, with optional filters, sort
	// and projection. The response carries the cursor the page was read
	// at, which is where a Watch should start.
	//
	// Auth: doc_read on the owning document.
	List(context.Context, *connect.Request[v1.ListRequest]) (*connect.Response[v1.ListResponse], error)
	// Mutate applies a list of row operations as one transaction and one
	// change batch. A cell write can carry the value it expects to replace;
	// a cell that no longer holds it is a conflict and keeps its value. So
	// is an operation on a row or column that was removed in the meantime.
	// By default a conflicting operation is skipped and reported while the
	// rest apply; with atomic set, any conflict fails them all.
	//
	// Auth: doc_write on the owning document.
	Mutate(context.Context, *connect.Request[v1.MutateRequest]) (*connect.Response[v1.MutateResponse], error)
	// Undo reverts a change batch, as a new batch. A cell changed by a
	// later batch is a conflict and keeps its value. Undo is offered only
	// within the change log window.
	//
	// Auth: doc_write on the owning document.
	Undo(context.Context, *connect.Request[v1.UndoRequest]) (*connect.Response[v1.UndoResponse], error)
	// Query runs read-only SQL against the views DescribeResponse lists,
	// which are named after the tables and columns rather than their ids.
	// It runs on a read-only connection that can read the views and the
	// catalog and nothing else, under a deadline, a row cap and a response
	// size cap, and is rate limited per subject. Results carry the catalog
	// types, so a client renders them like table rows.
	//
	// Returns invalid_argument for SQL that does not parse or reaches past
	// the views, and resource_exhausted on the rate limit or the deadline.
	//
	// Auth: doc_read on the owning document.
	Query(context.Context, *connect.Request[v1.QueryRequest]) (*connect.Response[v1.QueryResponse], error)
	// Changes reads the change log after a cursor: the unary catch-up for a
	// client that is not holding a Watch stream.
	//
	// Auth: doc_read on the owning document.
	Changes(context.Context, *connect.Request[v1.ChangesRequest]) (*connect.Response[v1.ChangesResponse], error)
	// Watch streams a database's changes after a cursor, as they commit,
	// together with presence, suggestions and heartbeats. The first message
	// is always a Hello carrying the stream's session id, which
	// UpdatePresence takes. A stream opened on a pod that does not own the
	// database is proxied to the owner.
	//
	// A refusal of the request comes before the first message, so it is
	// the call's status. Once open, the stream ends with one of three
	// reasons, carried in the error metadata under "reason":
	//
	//   lease_moved (code unavailable): the database moved to another pod,
	//   in a deploy or a drain. Reconnect with the last cursor received.
	//
	//   cursor_invalid (code failed_precondition): the cursor cannot be
	//   continued from. Either it is older than the oldest retained
	//   change, or it is from an older epoch and ahead of the seq the
	//   current epoch started from, so changes the client saw were lost in
	//   a crash of the previous owner, or it is from an epoch that
	//   DatabasesService.RecoverDatabase skipped. Reload the tables, then offer to
	//   re-apply the batches the client retained that the durable cursor
	//   had not passed, through Mutate with their original values as
	//   expected. Also the status of a Watch opened with such a cursor.
	//
	//   token_expired (code unauthenticated): the caller's token expired.
	//   Resume with a fresh token and the last cursor received, which runs
	//   the access check again.
	//
	// Auth: doc_read on the owning document.
	Watch(context.Context, *connect.Request[v1.WatchRequest]) (*connect.ServerStreamForClient[v1.WatchResponse], error)
	// Suggest proposes edits instead of making them, for agents, which
	// have no write scopes. It takes the same operations as Mutate, and
	// every cell write must carry the value it expects to replace, so that
	// a suggestion made stale by later edits fails per cell when applied
	// rather than overwriting them. The suggestion reaches editors on
	// Watch, and expires if nobody resolves it.
	//
	// Auth: the agent scope and doc_read on the owning document.
	Suggest(context.Context, *connect.Request[v1.SuggestRequest]) (*connect.Response[v1.SuggestResponse], error)
	// ResolveSuggestion applies or dismisses a suggestion. Applying runs it
	// as the caller's own Mutate, attributed to the caller with via set to
	// the agent that made it.
	//
	// Auth: doc_write on the owning document.
	ResolveSuggestion(context.Context, *connect.Request[v1.ResolveSuggestionRequest]) (*connect.Response[v1.ResolveSuggestionResponse], error)
	// ListSuggestions returns the open suggestions, so a client that opens
	// a table or reconnects starts from the full set, and Watch delivers
	// the rest.
	//
	// Auth: doc_read on the owning document.
	ListSuggestions(context.Context, *connect.Request[v1.ListSuggestionsRequest]) (*connect.Response[v1.ListSuggestionsResponse], error)
	// Summarize returns the distribution of one column without loading the
	// rows, for a table widget at card size. A COLUMN_TYPE_CHOICE or
	// COLUMN_TYPE_BOOLEAN column is counted per value. A COLUMN_TYPE_INTEGER,
	// COLUMN_TYPE_NUMBER, COLUMN_TYPE_DECIMAL, COLUMN_TYPE_DATE or
	// COLUMN_TYPE_DATETIME column is a histogram, with the buckets chosen by
	// the service: calendar units for dates. Decimal values are compared
	// exactly, so the bucket bounds, min, max and median of a decimal
	// column are exact, and a value on a bound is counted in the bucket
	// that bound starts. A bound beyond the range of an integer or a number
	// is clamped to that type's limit. Empty cells are counted separately,
	// and choice values beyond the bucket limit are counted together as
	// other.
	//
	// Text, multi-choice, JSON and document reference columns cannot be
	// summarised; a reference's label is a title the viewer may
	// not be allowed to read. Returns invalid_argument for such a column,
	// and failed_precondition when no column is given and the table has no
	// summary column.
	//
	// A card holds no Watch stream: it calls Summarize again, debounced,
	// when a data_changed or schema_changed event for the database arrives
	// on EventsService.WatchEvents.
	//
	// Auth: doc_read on the owning document.
	Summarize(context.Context, *connect.Request[v1.SummarizeRequest]) (*connect.Response[v1.SummarizeResponse], error)
	// UpdatePresence reports where the caller is looking or editing, for
	// the session of one of its own Watch streams. Presence is ephemeral:
	// it is not in the change log, and is gone when the stream ends.
	//
	// Auth: doc_read on the owning document, and the session must be one
	// of the caller's.
	UpdatePresence(context.Context, *connect.Request[v1.UpdatePresenceRequest]) (*connect.Response[v1.UpdatePresenceResponse], error)
}

